claim.claim-text:
1. Apparatus for holding a slidable body at a selected position intermediate fully retracted and fully extended positions with respect to a housing for the body, comprising:
a first latch element mounted to the housing adjacent the path traversed by the slidable body; and
a second latch element on the slidable body;
wherein one of the latch elements is mounted for movement into and out of engagement with the other latch element to hold the slidable body at an intermediate position defined by the other latch element;
and wherein said one latch element is biased either into or out of said engagement, and is movable against the bias from outside the housing.

17. A cabinet drawer comprising a cabinet housing and a drawer forming a slidable body mounted to be slidable in and out of the housing, and apparatus for holding the slidable body at a selected position intermediate fully retracted and fully extended positions with respect to a housing for the body, wherein the apparatus comprises:
a first latch element mounted to the housing adjacent the path traversed by the slidable body; and
a second latch element on the slidable body;
wherein one of the latch elements is mounted for movement into and out of engagement with the other latch element to hold the slidable body at an intermediate position defined by the other latch element;
and wherein said one latch element is biased either into or out of said engagement, and is movable against the bias from outside the housing.
